Rootlight third-party notices

Rootlight is distributed under the GNU Affero General Public License v3.0
only. The complete Rootlight license is bundled as LICENSE.

The release CycloneDX SBOM records the names, versions, sources, license
expressions, and dependency relationships of the Rust packages incorporated
into each platform artifact.

The local Web UI incorporates the exact npm dependency graph locked in
apps/rootlight-web/frontend/package-lock.json. The release bundle includes
licenses/rootlight-web-third-party-notices.txt, generated from that lockfile
and the license files carried by the exact installed packages. In particular,
the shipped @cosmos.gl/graph 3.4.0, @heroui/react 3.2.3, React 19.2.8, and
React DOM 19.2.8 packages each declare the MIT license. The generated notice
records a package declaration without inventing replacement text when an
upstream npm tarball omits its standalone license file.

The following Tree-sitter grammar crates omit a license file from their
published crate archives. Rootlight therefore bundles the exact license text
from each pinned upstream release under licenses/:

- tree-sitter-cpp 0.23.4
- tree-sitter-java 0.23.5
- tree-sitter-kotlin-ng 1.1.0
- tree-sitter-typescript 0.23.2

Their upstream repository, commit, license identifier, source URL, and
license-text checksum are pinned in adapters/grammars.lock.
